==================================================================
DAY 61 - PART A: THEORY
Custom Resource Definitions (CRDs)
Time: 40 minutes
==================================================================

1. EXTENDING THE API
--------------------
You've already used many CRDs: Certificate (cert-manager),
ServiceMonitor (Prometheus), Application (Argo CD), ScaledObject
(KEDA), CiliumNetworkPolicy. A CRD teaches the API server a NEW
resource type. After that, kubectl get/describe/apply/RBAC/watch all
work for it, and it is stored in etcd like built-ins.


2. A CRD
--------
  apiVersion: apiextensions.k8s.io/v1
  kind: CustomResourceDefinition
  metadata:
    name: websites.lab.example.com        # <plural>.<group>
  spec:
    group: lab.example.com
    scope: Namespaced
    names:
      kind: Website
      plural: websites
      singular: website
      shortNames: [ws]
    versions:
    - name: v1
      served: true
      storage: true
      schema:
        openAPIV3Schema: ...              # validation
      subresources:
        status: {}                        # separate status endpoint
      additionalPrinterColumns: ...       # columns in kubectl get


3. VALIDATION
-------------
openAPIV3Schema: types, required fields, enums, min/max, patterns,
defaults. Plus CEL rules (x-kubernetes-validations) for cross-field
checks, e.g. "self.replicas <= 10 || self.tier == 'premium'".
Invalid objects are rejected by the API server.


4. A CRD ALONE DOES NOTHING
---------------------------
It only stores data. A CONTROLLER watches the custom resources and
acts (creates Deployments, calls cloud APIs, ...). CRD + controller
with domain knowledge = OPERATOR (Day 62).
Controllers are usually written in Go with kubebuilder /
controller-runtime / Operator SDK; also possible in Python (kopf),
Java, or even shell (for learning).


5. VERSIONING
-------------
Multiple versions (v1alpha1, v1beta1, v1); one is the storage version;
conversion webhooks translate between them.


KEY POINTS TO REMEMBER
----------------------
- CRD = new API type with schema validation.
- Controller = the logic; CRD + controller = operator.
- Everything in kubectl works on custom resources.
